  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda - Farming, processing, distribution and sale of fish</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a financing from DGGF, FirstWave East Africa BV is enabled to set up a new production facility through its local subsidiary in Uganda.This Dutch company has years of experience in the breeding, processing and sale of fish. As part of a broader strategy, she wants to set up a new farm. The ambition is to grow and sell at least 30,000 tons of fish annually (in 7 years) on the local market. In order to realize this farm, they need to invest in a new production facility. The investment and activities that the company will carry out will have a significant development impact. In addition to the increase in local production, eventually (after 7 years) the investment will provide employment for approximately 600 employees, of which it is estimated that approximately 15% of the total number of employees will be women. The workers are trained in relation to the work they do. The company pays a good salary (including health insurance) and in addition, other things, such as travel costs, bonuses, etc. are offered to employees.</narrative>
  </description>
